<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine gas distributors approve bond program.</title>
<headline>Argentine gas distributors approve bond program.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine gas distributors Camuzzi Gas Pampeana SA and Camuzzi Gas del Sur SA said they have approved a joint non-convertible bond program of $200 million.</p>
<p>The companies said the issues will have maturities of up to five years. They have not decided whether the issues will be in pesos or other currencies or whether the bonds will be issued in the local market or abroad.</p>
<p>The gas distributors are owned by Italian industrial group Camuzzi.</p>
<p>-- Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0668</p>
